# acetohydroxamic_acid.msf
# Acetohydroxamic acid (CH3C(=O)NHOH)
# pKa=9.400 (N-H hydroxamic acid, q=0→-1)
# Source: Perrin 1981
# The acidic proton is on N-H (not O-H). Pure H+ loss from N-H:
# CH3C(=O)NHOH → CH3C(=O)N(OH)- + H+
# Important metal-chelating FG in drugs (vorinostat, deferiprone class).
# Fills pKa 9-10 with a completely new N-H pattern adjacent to C=O and OH.

